<title>USA: U.S. cotton ginnings - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton ginnings - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported all U.S. cotton ginnings with comparison (running bales, linters not included. W-withheld):</p>
<p>			1996	  1995</p>
<p>	  Al	59,550	 65,050</p>
<p>	  Az	50,400	 36,000</p>
<p>	  Ar     253,250	153,250</p>
<p>	  Ca	26,850	  7,600</p>
<p>	 Fla	   W		W</p>
<p>	  Ga     198,600	186,350</p>
<p>	  La     266,850	354,450</p>
<p>Cotton Ginnings continued -- (running bales):</p>
<p>			  1996	 1995</p>
<p> Ms		   480,500     564,000</p>
<p> Mo		    47,950	12,850</p>
<p> NM		     2,450	   Nil</p>
<p> NC		    21,600	23,000</p>
<p> Ok			 W	     Nil</p>
<p> SC		    61,750	15,850</p>
<p> Tn		   148,400	69,000</p>
<p> Tx		   518,400     954,550</p>
<p> US		 2,143,850   2,454,650</p>
<p>Cotton Ginnings continued --</p>
<p>USDA also reported American Pima cotton ginnings:</p>
<p>			  1996	     1995</p>
<p>	 Az		 W		 W</p>
<p>	 Ca		 W		 W</p>
<p>	 NM		 W		 W</p>
<p>	 TX		 W		 W</p>
<p> Other Sts	     Nil		Nil</p>
<p>	 U.S.	     W	     1,800</p>
<p>W - Withheld to avoid disclosing individual gins</p>
